<</Type/Catalog/Pages 1 0 R/Metadata 1031 0 R/Lang(en-US)/StructTreeRoot 24 0 R/MarkInfo<</Marked true/Suspects false>>/ViewerPreferences<</Direction/L2R>>/Outlines 23 0 R/Names<</Dests<</Names[(any-harm-to-defendants-from-reinstating-the-pandemic-unemployment-compensation-programs-is-far-outweighed-by-the-benefits-accruing-to-the-plaintiffs-and-other-unemployment-claimants)869 0 R(argument)861 0 R(as-demonstrated-by-correspondence-recently-sent-by-the-federal-department-of-labor-this-suit-is-not-moot)864 0 R(as-shown-above-plaintiffs-have-demonstrated-a-strong-likelihood-that-they-will-prevail-on-the-merits-of-this-case-and-the-court-must-therefore-turn-to-the-issue-of-harm-if-the-defendants-fail-to-reinstitute-the-program-within-a-short-time-however-this-assistance-will-become-permanently-unavailable-and-plaintiffs-will-suffer-irreparable-injury)867 0 R(because-of-the-public-interest-served-and-the-indigency-of-the-plaintiffs-this-court-should-not-require-any-of-the-plaintiffs-to-post-more-than-a-nominal-bond)871 0 R(conclusion)872 0 R(if-this-court-fails-to-issue-this-preliminary-injunction-there-will-be-no-adequate-remedy-at-law-for-the-plaintiffs-because-of-the-effects-of-the-pandemic-on-hundreds-of-thousands-of-alabamians-the-damage-caused-by-refusing-to-issue-the-injunction-will-greatly-outweigh-the-inconvenience-to-the-defendants)868 0 R(statement-of-jurisdiction)855 0 R(statement-of-the-case)856 0 R(statement-of-the-facts)858 0 R(statement-of-the-issues)857 0 R(statement-of-the-standard-of-review)859 0 R(statement-regarding-oral-argument)854 0 R(summary-of-the-argument)860 0 R(the-complaint-requests-relief-that-is-within-the-power-of-the-trial-court-to-grant-and-is-not-barred-by-sovereign-immunity-or-any-other-legal-defense)862 0 R(the-issuance-of-a-preliminary-injunction-serves-the-public-interest)870 0 R(the-plaintiffs-did-establish-the-criteria-requiring-issuance-of-a-preliminary-injunction-and-are-entitled-to-relief)866 0 R(this-suit-is-not-barred-by-laches)865 0 R(when-read-together-ala-code-25-4-118-and-ala-code-36-13-8-create-a-duty-in-the-governor-and-secretary-washington-to-fully-participate-in-unemployment-compensation-programs-offered-by-the-federal-government-since-this-is-a-mandatory-legal-duty-the-plaintiffs-request-fits-within-a-defined-exception-to-the-defendants-sovereign-immunity)863 0 R(xd-lh)873 0 R]>>>>>>
